# <%= module.title %> CRUD Draft

Generated by `corepack pnpm generate:module` or the Web module generator.

This is a reviewable draft. Web-generated drafts stay offline in `generated/module-drafts` until you
publish them from `/system/module/generator`. Publishing applies the reviewed snippets and files into
the real project source.

## Target Files

| Piece | Target |
| --- | --- |
| Schema snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.schema %>` |
| Migration snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.migration %>` |
| Backend route | `<%= module.targetPaths.route %>` |
| Route registration snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.systemRoute %>` |
| Feature page | `<%= module.targetPaths.feature %>` |
| App Router page | `<%= module.targetPaths.appPage %>` |
| Route manifest snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.routeManifest %>` |
| Seed rule snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.seedRule %>` |
| API acceptance snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.apiTestCases %>` |
| Page acceptance snippet | `<%= module.targetPaths.pageTestCases %>` |
| API test | `<%= module.targetPaths.test %>` |

## Publish Or Apply

For a Web draft, use the per-file diff in `/system/module/generator`. The reviewed plan hash must
still match before isolated preflight and source publication can start. Do not copy the files by
hand before using that flow.

For a CLI-only draft, apply the artifacts manually in this order:

1. Apply the schema and migration snippets.
2. Copy the backend route, feature page, App Router page, and API test.
3. Apply the system-route, route-manifest, and seed-rule snippets; review the rule ID.
4. Apply the API/page acceptance snippets to the generator-owned sections in
   `tests/coverage/generated-module-test-cases.ts`.

After publication, these files are repository-owned source. Regeneration is diff-only and must not
overwrite hand-written changes.

